  "query_preview": "..\n(Monday through Thursday)\nIssued at 205 AM CST Fri Nov 27 2026\n\nThe weather pattern becomes more zonal aloft after Saturday's\nupper trough moves east and we will have a warming trend into\nmid-week next week. A strong upper low is forecast to move onshore\nover southern California Tuesday/Wednesday, open up and move\ntoward the southern Plains late in the week, although the specific\ntiming is still somewhat in question. The operational 00Z ECMWF is\nquicker to open this low up into a trough and quicker to move it\ntoward the Plains while the operational 00Z GFS is slower on both\naccounts. But regardless, precipitation chances go up towards\nWednesday night or Thursday as this system approaches with a cold\nfront and cooling trend after it moves by. But this airmass is not\ntoo cold and the temperatures late in the week are still expected\nto be near seasonal averages.",
